7 Key Steps for a Successful CI/CD Pipeline 🔥

A CI/CD pipeline automates the process from development to production, ensuring efficiency and stability. Let’s explore the 7 key phases of a CI/CD workflow

1️⃣ Code Integration
Frequent integration to avoid merge conflicts.
Trigger automated validation to maintain branch stability.

2️⃣ Build
Compile code, install dependencies, and prepare for testing.
Cache dependencies and use parallel tasks to speed up the process.

3️⃣ Testing
Run automated tests (unit, integration, end-to-end).
Focus on comprehensive coverage and optimized speed.

4️⃣ Pre-Release Environment
Simulate the production environment to detect issues.
Use Infrastructure as Code (IaC) to ensure environment consistency.

5️⃣ Pre-Release Testing
Run performance, security, and QA tests.
Verify app readiness for deployment.

6️⃣ Production
Deploy the application to the live environment.
Use monitoring and logging to track performance.

7️⃣ Track and Log
Continuously monitor system health and performance.
Implement clear logs and real-time alerting.

CI/CD Best Practices

▪️Automate every step of the pipeline.
▪️Simplify processes for faster delivery.
▪️Maintain consistency across environments.
▪️Optimize speed of builds and tests.
▪️Monitor continuously to quickly address issues.
